{"assets":["/statement-assets/20b9ecbf0572b2991aa9ac8092fb390efd2956725ac79b2227844f1009ea06df.png","/statement-assets/b3add51d02f47289f99441a0b3c1e8291ab2fccbd9e1475e1a099a8084823818.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1178","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F2. Long Colorful Strip"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"6 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is the second subtask of problem F. The only differences between this and the first subtask are the constraints on the value of $$$m$$$ and the time limit. It is sufficient to solve this subtask in order to hack it, but you need to solve both subtasks in order to hack the first one."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$n+1$$$ distinct colours in the universe, numbered $$$0$$$ through $$$n$$$. There is a strip of paper $$$m$$$ centimetres long initially painted with colour $$$0$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice took a brush and painted the strip using the following process. For each $$$i$$$ from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"in this order"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", she picks two integers $$$0 \\leq a_i \\lt b_i \\leq m$$$, such that the segment $$$[a_i, b_i]$$$ is currently painted with a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"single"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" colour, and repaints it with colour $$$i$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice chose the segments in such a way that each centimetre is now painted in some colour other than $$$0$$$. Formally, the segment $$$[i-1, i]$$$ is painted with colour $$$c_i$$$ ($$$c_i \\neq 0$$$). Every colour other than $$$0$$$ is visible on the strip."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Count the number of different pairs of sequences $$$\\{a_i\\}_{i=1}^n$$$, $$$\\{b_i\\}_{i=1}^n$$$ that result in this configuration. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Since this number may be large, output it modulo $$$998244353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a two integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 500$$$, $$$n \\leq m \\leq 10^6$$$) — the number of colours excluding the colour $$$0$$$ and the length of the paper, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$m$$$ space separated integers $$$c_1, c_2, \\ldots, c_m$$$ ($$$1 \\leq c_i \\leq n$$$) — the colour visible on the segment $$$[i-1, i]$$$ after the process ends. It is guaranteed that for all $$$j$$$ between $$$1$$$ and $$$n$$$ there is an index $$$k$$$ such that $$$c_k = j$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output a single integer — the number of ways Alice can perform the painting, modulo $$$998244353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 3\n1 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 3\n1 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 3\n2 1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7 7\n4 5 1 6 2 3 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n165\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8 17\n1 3 2 2 7 8 2 5 5 4 4 4 1 1 6 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n20\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, there are $$$5$$$ ways, all depicted in the figure below. Here, $$$0$$$ is white, $$$1$$$ is red, $$$2$$$ is green and $$$3$$$ is blue."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/20b9ecbf0572b2991aa9ac8092fb390efd2956725ac79b2227844f1009ea06df.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Below is an example of a painting process that is not valid, as in the second step the segment "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 3"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not single colour, and thus may not be repainted with colour $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b3add51d02f47289f99441a0b3c1e8291ab2fccbd9e1475e1a099a8084823818.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, Alice must first paint segment "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0 3"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" with colour $$$1$$$ and then segment "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" with colour $$$2$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F2","problemCode":"1178F2","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1178/problem/F2"}